.TH R_MEMPOOL_ALLOC_ENTRY 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
r_mempool_alloc_entry \- allocate an entry from the ranged pool
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <cmempool.h>

void *r_mempool_alloc_entry(r_mempool *rmp, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Allocates memory of the requested size from the most appropriate sub-pool.
The size is rounded up to the nearest power-of-2 pool. If the optimal pool
is exhausted, tries larger pools. Fallback behavior depends on policy.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
rmp   Ranged memory pool to allocate from
size  Size in bytes to allocate (must be > 0 and <= largest_size)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Returns pointer to allocated entry on success
Returns NULL on failure
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(1) in common case, O(number_of_pools) worst case
Returned memory is uninitialized (use r_mempool_calloc_entry() for zeroed)
Size is rounded up to next power-of-2 pool size
Tries progressively larger pools if optimal pool is exhausted
Thread-safe if pool created with single_threaded=false
Entry must be freed with r_mempool_free_entry()
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR r_mempool_calloc_entry (3),
.BR r_mempool_realloc_entry (3),
.BR r_mempool_free_entry (3)
